{
  "_comment": [
    "A small, realistic sample of Congress.gov API v3 house-vote responses, in",
    "the field shapes documented live at",
    "https://github.com/LibraryOfCongress/api.congress.gov/blob/main/Documentation/HouseRollCallVoteEndpoint.md",
    "(fetched 2026-10-16) and cross-checked against",
    "https://blogs.loc.gov/law/2025/05/introducing-house-roll-call-votes-in-the-congress-gov-api/",
    "and a live, unauthenticated probe of https://api.congress.gov/v3/house-vote/118/2/452",
    "which confirmed the URL scheme and that api.congress.gov is reachable (it",
    "returned API_KEY_MISSING, not a DNS or routing failure) -- see story 5.1's",
    "PR for the probe. No real API key was available this session, so this file",
    "is a hand-built approximation of the real shape, not a captured live",
    "response: field names and enum values are taken directly from the cited",
    "documentation; specific vote counts, bill numbers and dates are invented",
    "but internally consistent, and the roll numbers/congress/session match",
    "datamodel.md's own worked example id `us-house:119-2:452`.",
    "",
    "The real API's JSON uses the same camelCase field names as the XML tags",
    "the doc describes (confirmed by Congress.gov API convention across every",
    "other endpoint this repo already ingests against, e.g. bill/member), with",
    "list results wrapped under a plural container key and item results under",
    "the singular -- mirrored here as houseRollCallVotes / houseRollCallVote.",
    "",
    "Used by tests/step_defs/test_house_rollcalls_steps.py and",
    "tests/test_house_rollcalls_unit.py. Never fetched over the network in CI."
  ],

